imes require  optimizations in the workflow so it's  possible that  that the the workflow may actually take  even  a few days longer now considering that  it is quite critical especially for  newly diagnosed advanced non-small cell  lung cancer to get a molecular profile  as quickly as possible  of course we are very interested in  trying to get this  turnaround time as short as possible and  optimize it  even further in fact this is why we were  very happy to hear  about the new genexo system which  promises  uh turnaround time as short as one day  to get from sample to report so of  course we really wanted to try this  and luckily we had the opportunity over  the last six months or so to  uh to extensively test this system  and uh we can he confirmed that that  we can get ngs results uh  in as short as one day in addition the  full  the workflow from library prep to data  analysis is now fully automated so it  requires  very little hands-on uh very little  technical knowledge  about it um plus it is more flexible in  terms of throughput as our current  system with the iron chef  and the s5  so if we go back to those five steps  to the workflow that currently takes us  four to five working days  now the difference is with this system  we're actually able  to take the last three steps and put  them all together  fully automated on the genexo system  so of course this will shorten the  turnaround time because in fact the  processes that are happening fully uh  automated uh are also done quicker than  if we do it manually  eventually resulting in a turnaround  time of one to two days  so in real life the instrument looks  like this this is a photo from our  test laboratory in our institute just  for comparison you have  on the left side you have the iron shift  and the ins five  and then of course in the in the in the  middle the  genexo sequencer now if we look on the  deck  of this those of you familiar with the  iron chef for example  it will look familiar to you  