recision  assay running on the uh  torrent genexo system uh  the labs that participated here are  lower  were located in berlin in porto in  naples and  of course us in basel and in fact you  will hear about the results of this  multicentric evaluation in the talk  by michael hummel later today  so until then i would like to show you  also some results but some results on  very specific sample types that we are  facing in the lab and i believe that  many labs are are facing uh challenges  with  so in particular i'm talking about very  low  tumor cellularity cytological specimens  so if we look at the vast  variety of day-to-day samples that we  receive of course on the on the very  left you can see  we uh we we get resections  and those are what i would consider uh  the easy samples we have a lot of  material we can get a lot of dna rna out  of it  quality is quite okay and usually not  very challenging to perform ngs on those  where it gets more challenging is more  when we go  in the direction of biopsies actually  very small biopsies where we have very  little material and we still need to  be able to to to get the high quality  results out of an ngs  analysis and you also see here in the  middle  psychology samples cytology samples  often are  quite low cellularity meaning we have  less than 20  tumor cells and what we do in our  institutes  if we have less less than 20 percent  tumor cell content we perform laser  capture micro dissection  in order to specifically enrich tumor  cells from which we then isolate  nucleic acid and perform ngs  and these cytology samples i would like  to talk a little bit more about  and show you some some exciting results  later  so in switzerland  if we look at all the diagnosed  non-small cell lung cancers  in fact we have 40 percent of these  diagnosis that are being done on  psychology samples so they  are actually play a major part in our  day-to-day  uh activity in our laboratory and of  course  we need to adapt our ngs workflow but we  still want to be able to  to to provide useful results for those  despite having low tumor cell contents  often uh these samples also have some  advantages  over over uh formally in fixed histology  samples and that  major advantage is that cytology symbols  are not fixed informally in like  histology symbols but rather in alcohol  based fixatives and this has the  advantage that we do not have to deal  with formally induced deamination  artifacts  uh meaning we can actually potentially  call variants at the lower allelic  frequency without  without having too much noise from these  deamination artifacts  so as i mentioned many  psychological smears that we get in our  day-to-day  life in the lab often have uh  less than 20 tumor cells in fact it's  around 50 percent  as as as you can see here and in this 50  of all cytology samples we perform laser  capture micro dissection  now this basically results in as i  mentioned before in  enrichment of specific tumor cells but  as you can see on the right we  usually enrich for about two to three  hundred cells which are very few cells  uh and of course we will get very little  uh  nucleic acid material out of it and  despite this  we're usually still able to provide uh  an ngs result in most of the cases but  of course it does  it does uh result in some challenges  in data analysis also it is quite time  consuming to perform this uh  micro by section plus of course it is  expensive because we have to invest in a  in a separate infrastructure for the  example  while the samples with more than 20  tumor cell content  we basically uh we can scrape off with a  scalpel  just like from from other samples from  tissue  samples which is quick gives us a lot of  material  and is cost efficient  so we were actually  quite happy to see together with the new  uh  sequencer to also have a new assay which  is the oncoming precision assay  and just very quickly i don't want to go  into too much detail but  basically it's a 