 family which is  present on only one member  so here we know this is very likely an  artifact and we would filter it out  because if it were a true  variant it would be present of course  on the original template molecule in our  input dna  and it should be present in all the  family members because all these family  members with the red  umi are copies of that  specific molecule so here we know this  is an artifact while the  the light blue star we can see they are  present in all family members  in a family and therefore it's very  likely to be a true variant  so this really enhances sensitivity and  specificity and allows us and yet to get  to a limit of detection of  around between 0.1 and 0.5 percent  allelic frequency  so if you now go back to this workflow  what we're hoping now is that with this  technology  we do not have to perform laser capture  micro dissection anymore for the load  cellularity samples but instead actually  we can now for all of the samples that  we have we can  do manual collection we can scrape off  all the cells  we get a lot of material we use the  precision assay  on the genexo sequencer to also get the  shortest turnaround time  and to get these results as quickly as  possible  so we started to test this and what i  show you here  are three different samples you see here  three  cytology smears two of which have an  estimated tumor cell content of ten  percent and one  uh at five percent  from all of these samples we had we  previously had additional smears  which we had later microdissected  uh and then sequenced so you can see in  the table below  for all three samples we had identified  different mutations so we have an egfr  l858r and egfr exo19 deletion as well as  the keras g12c  um in the in the  in in the column lcm af you can see the  allylic frequency of these  variants as they were detected when we  enrich tumor cells with laser capture  microtransaction and on the far right  the last column you can see that  all three mutations were detected  without laser capture micro dissection  when we used  the oncoming precision assay and you can  see that two of them were at  very low allelic frequencies around two  percent  uh usually for tissue we don't go below  three or five percent allelic frequency  so here we can see that we can actually  uh uh  get below that and very importantly of  course we did not detect any false  positives  in these samples at this range of  of a detection limit  last thing that i want to show you is  another experiment where we wanted to go  we wanted to test even further how  low can we go in terms of allelic  frequency in terms of limit of detection  so we took two samples again which has  been previously characterized  one are having a pic3ca hrs and pp53  mutation  and the second sample having an egfr  mutation and what we did now is we took  sample number one  and we diluted this with sample number  two in a dilution series  this you can see here in the bottom you  can see  in the first column the undiluted sample  number one  where we detect with the oncoming  precision assay  the pic3c8hs and tp53 mutation  but not of course the egfr but once we  start to dilute sample one with sample  two that has tgfr  we can see that the egf-4 starts to come  up and  at the same time the the mutations of  sample 1  start to get more and more diluted  now to make long story short if you go  all the way to the right  uh 1 to 32 dilution in fact  we're still able to detect all three  mutations of sample 1  bound to an allylic frequency of around  1  uh again even at this dilution we  detected  no uh additional artifacts or false  positives  but it will save we so we retained the  specificity  um and at the same time uh have a very  high  sensitivity so this based on these  results this is very promising of course  we're testing this  with with uh more samples now but we're  already quite happy and  hopefully in the future we can avoid  laser capture micro dissection  by employing this assay that is using uh  molecular tagging technology  so with this i would like to summarize  our experience with the  genexos system so three major points i  would like to point out  very short turnaround time  indeed we can now get from sample  to result in even less than one day so  shortest run time is 13 hours  uh longest run time if we if we if we  run the full chip at once with 16 dna  rna samples  is 30 hours but in the end  this will allow us to deliver our ngs  results hopefully together  even with our immunohistochemistry  results  second is very easy to use it requires  almost no hands-on  it requires very little bioinformatics  knowledge since the analysis pipeline is  part of  the of the automated workflow um it's an  all-in-one box so it can be easily set  up in any laboratory  and last but not least we were quite  happy with the  new precision assay employing molecular  barcoding and allowing us to hopefully  avoid  laser capture micro dissection by  offering higher sensitivity  and specificity than  other library assays  and with this i would like to thank the  team at our institute  involved in this project i would like to  thank of course also thermal fisher  for giving me the opportunity to present  our data here and of course i would like  to thank you the audience  for your attention and i will be very  happy to open  to answer questions
 

